seen the eldians can go there in  particular circumstances  these paths that we see in the sky are  the things that connect every single ld  into the founding titan and in zeke's  case since he has real blood his  connection to the founder is more  special than other aldians for that  reason the girl chose to save him  specifically because he has royal blood  and as the season continues his  connection to her will be explained in  greater detail but for now this is all  we need to know  when it comes to the situation with the  jaegerus in the previous episode hanji  was being forced to take them to zeke's  location but after hearing the sound of  a thunderspear flock decided to change  directions so they could investigate  this is how the yageras were able to  find levi and zeke in his open field and  after being hit with a thunder spirit  close range the captain was undeniably  in the worst shape of his life  besides the fact that he was  unresponsive and covered in blood he had  also lost two fingers that were still  attached to the trigger of his equipment  what was interesting about this scene is  just how much the jaegers wanted to make  sure he was dead cause until this moment  they assumed that the captain would try  to stop them from bringing zeke back to  shiganchina and you know what if he was  conscious he probably would have this is  the reason why hanji tried to claim that  levi was dead so that maybe they'd leave  him alone but one zeke emerged she had  no choice but to try and escape to put  it simply there's no way the beast titan  would have allowed his greatest enemy  who's defeated him you know two or three  times now there's no way he could have  allowed him to survive so by hanji  jumping into the river with the captain  it at least gives him some chance of  staying alive  now switching over to mali's surprise  attack on shigachina at the start of the  episode the malians had two main  objectives the first objective was for  either rhino or poco to eat the founding  titan while pique was meant to provide  support with this special anti-titan  cannon the cannon was dropped into the  district as soon as the invasion began  and in this screenshot you can see that  she saw it coming from a distance which  is how peak knew exactly where she  needed to go unfortunately at this time  she'd been handcuffed to gabby so she  wasn't immediately able to transform  since her titan explosion would have  likely killed the warrior candidate  that's why the draw titan had to sever  off her hand so that these two could be  separated and in the process the card  titan was then able to manifest  one small piece of trivia to mention is  that in the very first episode of the  season you'll remember that these  anti-tank cannons were actually  developed by the middle eastern alliance  and molly just stole them after winning  the war hence why it's now been modified  to fit the cart titan  anyway general mcgath's secondary  objective was to rescue gabby and falco  and his reaction to seeing gabby again  was very emotional for amalian  especially considering this is the same  guy who sent hundreds if not thousands  of eldians to their deaths i mean in the  first episode he was literally about to  sacrifice 800 of them  when it comes to falco's location he was  still locked up in a prison cell along  with the other soldiers who drank zeke  spawn of fluid and it was now cult's  responsibility to go and find his  younger brother  just before we move on to eren's fight  with reiner it's worth pointing out that  for the first time ever marley finally  realized that zeke might be a titan of  royal blood after gabby remembered what  he said on the airship this means that  on top of everything else their new  objective is also to stop zeke from  making contact with aaron  in terms of what aaron himself was  thinking early in the episode he was  just surprised that marley was able to  launch a counter-attack so soon given  that he had wiped out all of their top  military officials despite that it was  thanks to reina's persistence that  marley went ahead with this invasion  only one month later and it didn't take  aaron long to realize he was responsible  the armored titan then parachutes into  the city which was reminiscent of what  he did at forslava only this time around  he's also joined by hundreds of other  malian soldiers  during that fight the anime definitely  answered the question of who has the  better titan hardening cause rhino  literally tried to break through aaron's  defenses over 10 times with no success  only for aaron to then just break  through his armor in one punch i just  think they need to come up with a brand  new name for this shifter because it  seems like the armor crumbles every  single time he's in a real contest  in any case with rhino on the ground  galia tried to sneak up on the attack  titan in a moment that parallels what he  did in liberia and as he went in for the  kill we got to see aaron's war hammer  titan abilities his first move was to  create huge spikes of titan hardening  that were literally coming out of his  actual body which is a way we've not  exactly seen his power used before  regardless of that galliard quickly  swiped it all away because the draw  titan is essentially the natural enemy  of the warhammer as the fight continued  eren was backed into a corner where he  had to use more substantial amounts of  hardening to defend himself and in  fairness he was able to push back the  two warriors with reiner looking  especially messed up  the slight downside with this game plan  is that the warhammer's abilities do  drain energy pretty quickly as we saw  with lara tiber so it's usually a smart  move not to overdo it  anyhow with reiner and galliard  suspended in the air mcgath provides him  with the assist by firing through the  founding titan's brain by doing this  aaron needs time to regenerate before  his titan can move again giving the  warriors an 