e tiger said that  marley needed another hero and the way  this scene is set up is implied that  that hero could in fact be reiner this  is funny considering that reiner's early  motivations back in the day was to be a  hero that could save the world and now  after a lot of mistakes he's now  stumbled into a position where he can  seemingly still achieve that goal  now moving down to the prison cells  onyankapon wanted to release armin  mikasa and the other prisoners so they  could lend their strength to try and  save eren in previous seasons it would  have been almost guaranteed that they'd  agreed to help but connie and drawn  rightly point out that helping aaron  also means helping with zeke's  euthanization plan  i explained this in my review of the  first half of the season but basically  aaron agreed to help zeke peacefully end  the aldian race by using his founding  titan to remove their ability to  reproduce that philosophy is not  something anyone in this room would  really want to risk their lives for so  you can understand why they'd be  skeptical in helping out however in this  episode armin comes to the realization  that maybe aaron doesn't actually  believe in this kind of euthanization  and he's just pretending to follow zeke  and yell in his plan  after all way back in season one when we  got to see inside aaron's mind he said  the reason he wanted to explore the  outside and acquire freedom is because  he was born into this world so why would  he then want to stop future generations  from being born it doesn't make sense  that he would spend years fighting for  freedom only to then deny that same  freedom to future aldians so armin does  make a good point that maybe aaron is  just playing along  if the two brothers make contact then  it's ultimately aaron's decision how the  founding titan will be used meaning that  he doesn't really have to follow the  euthanization plan if he doesn't want to  what ahmed is essentially saying here is  that they need to take a chance to save  aaron and just hope that he's really on  their side  on a separate note he also theorizes  that the idea of mikasiv being  controlled by her ackman dna is another  lie that eren made up although in this  case he doesn't provide an explanation  as to why he thinks it's not true all we  know is that in the last episode it was  suggested that there might be a hidden  motive behind why he said these things  but for now that's all we got  anyway the episode ends with elder  soldiers still getting destroyed on the  surface and i gotta say the anime has  really elevated the level of like  graphic-ness and bloodiness of this  conflict because in the manga we legit  didn't see anywhere close to this number  of soldiers being killed  with that said that was my breakdown for  episode 17 of attack on time season four  and it's been many many months since my  last review so i'd appreciate if you  dropped a like hit that sub button if  you haven't already and let me know in  the comments what you thought of the  episode  until the next one peace out

